          allows_nulls: false,
          column_type: "Metric",
          data_type: "Decimal",
          description_md: "The *amortized* cost of the *charge* after applying all reduced rates, discounts, and the applicable portion of relevant, prepaid purchases (one-time or recurring) that covered this *charge*.\n\n### Concerning Granularity and Distribution of Recurring Fee\n\nProviders should distribute the *commitment* purchase amount instead of including a *row* at the beginning of a period so practitioners do not need to manually distribute the fee themselves.\n\n### Concerning Amortization Approaches\n\nEligible purchases should be *amortized* using a methodology determined by the provider that reflects the needs of their customer base and is proportional to the Pricing Quantity and the time granularity of the *row*. Should a practitioner desire to *amortize* relevant purchases using a different approach, the practitioner can do so using the [Billed Cost](#billedcost) for the line item representing the initial purchase.",
          display_name: "Effective Cost",
          feature_level: "Mandatory",
          id: "EffectiveCost",
          introduced_version: "0.5",
